# Mechanism: from-uv-tool — Python CLI tools via uv tool install.
# Realizer: src/Core.TypeScript/ace/setup-realizers/from-uv-tool.ts
# non-empty line; optional `==X.Y.Z` version qualifier per line.
#
# Zeta scope (today): ruff for Python linting of any Python helper
# scripts that land under `tools/`. Semgrep is NOT here — Semgrep is
# a dotnet-install-managed dep (see `common/dotnet-tools.sh`) that
# happens to be written in Python, not a uv-installed tool.
#
# Single flat manifest today; `@include` hierarchy (@min in @all)
# is a BACKLOG P1 item.

# PINNED, and pinned to the SAME version .mise.toml pins. A bare `ruff` here means
# `uv tool install ruff` fetches latest and OVERWRITES the mise-installed pin
# seconds after it lands. Measured in `lint (Python)` on main 2026-08-29:
#
#     pipx:ruff 0.15.17        <- mise installs the pin
#     ...
#     uv tool install ruff...
#      + ruff==0.16.5          <- overwritten, unpinned
#
# That matters because the bump is a lint-POLICY change, not a version change:
# .mise.toml records that against this tree ruff 0.15.17 says "All checks passed!"
# and 0.16.4 says "Found 65 errors." So the job ran a ruff the tree was never green
# against. The failure is intermittent (6/60 runs) only because the realizer's
# already-installed check matches on NAME alone, so a warm cache skips the
# overwrite and a cold one does not.
#
# Keep in sync with `"pipx:ruff"` in .mise.toml. The deeper defect that .mise.toml
# names -- src/Core.Python/pyproject.toml has no [tool.ruff], so the rule set is
# "whatever ruff defaults to this month" -- is NOT fixed here; pinning the tool in
# both places is the prerequisite, not the cure.
ruff==0.15.17
